METH["overall"] = [
    ("h2", "6.1 Overall Methodology"),
    ("p", "The methodology has seven stages that mirror the workflow in Chapter 5. (1) A seeded generator produces a GST ecosystem with injected, labelled fraud and legitimate hard negatives. (2) Three layers of features (invoice, return behaviour and network) are computed for every active taxpayer-month. (3) A JEPA encoder is trained, without labels, to predict the embedding of a month from the embeddings of the previous three months and from the month itself with one feature layer hidden; the prediction error is the deviation score. (4) The trade graph is searched for short recurring cycles and for registrations that share an address or contact number. (5) Every invoice receives a noisy-OR anomaly score from eight weighted signals. (6) The four layer scores are combined into one risk per taxpayer, taxpayers and invoice chains are ranked, and patterns and evidence are derived. (7) Gemini writes a cited case note from the evidence on request, and the result is checked. Evaluation against the injected labels and against a rule baseline is run on the same scores ({fig:algo})."),
    ("fig", "algo", ALGO, "Flowchart of the core algorithm (risk scoring)", 4.9),
]

