METH["pipeline"] = [
    ("h2", "6.7 Network, Invoice and Risk Pipeline"),
    ("p", "`ml/pipeline.py` strings the stages together. After the JEPA scores, it builds the directed trade graph (edge attributes: total value, tax, count, months and unreported value) and runs the bounded cycle search; on the bundled ecosystem 79 candidate cycles were scanned, which merged into 9 rings, 7 of which contain injected-fraud taxpayers. It then builds identity clusters (12 clusters in total, 7 suspicious), scores each invoice, forms the layer scores, combines them and ranks the taxpayers."),
    ("p", "**Patterns.** A flagged taxpayer is given a named pattern from the evidence: *circular trading* if it belongs to a ring; *shell entity* if it is in a suspicious cluster and is young, has stopped filing or pays almost no cash tax; *fake invoices* if it is not a shell entity but buys from suspicious clusters (10 % of purchases or more in some month) or has at least 15 % of purchase value flagged; *ITC spike* if a month's claim is at least 2.5 times its median, above Rs 1 lakh and at least 1.5 times the available credit; and *unusual behaviour* if nothing else applies but the JEPA score is at least 0.5."),
    ("p", "**Evidence.** For every taxpayer, up to eleven kinds of evidence item are produced with a layer, a severity and concrete numbers: JEPA deviation with the three largest feature shifts, months where the GSTR-3B claim exceeds GSTR-2B, ITC spikes, low cash payment against the sector median, suspicious purchase and sales invoices, ring membership with the loop path, the shared-identity cluster, exposure to shell suppliers, stopped filing and high turnover soon after registration. Items are sorted by severity and numbered E1 to En."),
    ("p", "**Invoice chains.** Each detected ring and each suspicious cluster (together with its buyers) becomes a chain with a score built from the ring or cluster score and the risk of its members or the anomalous share of its invoices. On the bundled ecosystem there are 16 chains."),
]

